  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Committed enqueue",
      "items": [
        "the state change and the outbox row live in one DB transaction — never enqueue a job whose DB write failed, never commit a change whose job was lost",
        "the row, not the Redis job, is the durability boundary: Redis down degrades enqueueing but committed data stays safe"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Claim + relay",
      "items": [
        "bin/worker.ts claims due queued rows with jittered polling and bumps each one into a BullMQ job keyed on the outbox id",
        "the same worker file runs the janitor loop on one AbortController; consumers are idempotent — a retried job must not double-send"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Outcomes",
      "items": [
        "retries use capped exponential backoff (attempts + exponential with a ceiling) — a poison job dead-letters instead of looping forever",
        "settle marks the row sent or failed with last_error, so a dead-lettered job is visible in the table and logs, never silently dropped",
        "the worker's status changes are its own structured log lines — the claim → send → retry/dead-letter progression tells the story"
      ]
    }
  ]
}